{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClockUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClockUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.CharZero.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.borel_identification_core","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.borel_identification_core","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L283-L311","doc":"**The composed reduction (proved, sorry-free, conditional).** GIVEN\n(1) the one-clock conjecture (class hypothesis), (2) that the binding and\nloop counters are clocks, (3) the shared-variable representability\npremise `hrep` — for whatever scale relates the two clocks, the binding\nnormalizer is the loop-moment sequence read scale-covariantly in the\nbinding chart (OPEN; this is the analytic-representability face of the\nidentification, restricted to its arithmetic shadow) — and (4) the\nLean-proved keystone identity (`hkey`), the binding normalizer IS the\nunit factorial sequence: `N(m+1) = m!`. This conclusion is verbatim the\n`moment_eq_normalizer` field of `BorelProperTimeIdentification`\n(content-block sibling of `conj:schwinger-measure-computational-time`)\nat unit `ς = 1` — the conjecture's algebraic core, now a CONSEQUENCE of\none-clock + representability + the proved keystone. What is NOT supplied:\nthe analytic fields (`positive`, `integrable`) of\n`BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation` — kernel representability stays\nopen; see the file header's reduction chain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.scale_and_unit_pinned_of_keystone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.scale_and_unit_pinned_of_keystone","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L241-L281","doc":"**Keystone kills both parameters (proved, sorry-free,\nunconditional).** If the binding normalizer is the loop-moment sequence\nread scale-covariantly at relative clock scale `lam` with measure unit\n`ς` — `N(m+1) = lam^{m+1}·ς·m!` — and the Lean-proved keystone identity\n`n·N(n) = n!` holds (`KeystoneBridgeC1Binding`, hypothesis `hkey` per the\n`_of_` discipline), then the scale AND the unit are both forced:\n`lam = 1 ∧ ς = 1`. Two moments decide it: `m = 0` gives `lam·ς = 1`;\n`m = 1` gives `lam²·ς = 1`, hence `lam = 1`, hence `ς = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.clocks_agree_up_to_scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.clocks_agree_up_to_scale","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L228-L239","doc":"**Conditional clock-level core (proved, sorry-free).** GIVEN the\none-clock conjecture, the binding side's Borel/jet-level counter `Tb` and\nthe loop's proper-time counter `Ts` — both clocks of the same\ncomputation monoid under owner premise P2 — agree up to a nonzero scale.\nThis is the clock-level core of the Borel/proper-time identification:\nwhat separates the two sectors' time variables is at most the single\nscale P1 quotients out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.unique_up_to_scale_of_atomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.unique_up_to_scale_of_atomic","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L198-L226","doc":"**Discharge map (proved, sorry-free).** The one-clock statement HOLDS\nfor any step monoid generated by a single atomic step: if every\ncomputation is an iterate of one generator `g` (`∀ a, ∃ n, a = n • g` —\nthe formal shape of \"no sub-step resolution\",\n`rem:discrete-planck-step`), then any two clocks differ by a nonzero\nscale. This is the exact open premise the primary conjecture reduces to:\nATOMICITY of the substrate's computation monoid. Stated as a plain\ntheorem, NOT an instance — instantiating the class at the substrate's\nmonoid requires proving that monoid's atomicity, which is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.uniqueness_fails_for_two_generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.uniqueness_fails_for_two_generators","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L175-L196","doc":"**Non-tautology witness (proved, unconditional).** The one-clock\nstatement is FALSE for the rank-two step monoid `ℕ × ℕ`: the two\ncoordinate counters are both clocks but are not proportional. Hence\n`SubstrateClockUniqueness` carries real content — it asserts the\nsubstrate's computation monoid does NOT decompose into independent\nparallel step-counting directions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.SubstrateClockUniqueness.unique_up_to_scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.SubstrateClockUniqueness.unique_up_to_scale","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L171-L171","doc":"Any two clocks differ by a nonzero scale: the substrate's\ncomputational time is unique up to the P1-quotiented scale action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.SubstrateClockUniqueness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.SubstrateClockUniqueness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L167-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.SubstrateClockUniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.SubstrateClockUniqueness","kind":"class","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L153-L173","doc":"**Primary conjecture (open — NO instance; §3b-tax).** THE SUBSTRATE\nHAS ONE CLOCK: any two clocks of the substrate's computation monoid\ndiffer by a single nonzero scale — the scale freedom that owner premise\nP1 (substrate scale-freedom) already quotients out. The field is\nparameter-quantified over all clock pairs; it is a genuine structural\nrestriction on `M` (rank-one-ness of the computation monoid), FALSE for a\ntwo-generator step monoid (`uniqueness_fails_for_two_generators`) and\ndischarged by atomicity of the step monoid\n(`unique_up_to_scale_of_atomic` — the \"no sub-step resolution\" of the\nPlanck step, `rem:discrete-planck-step`, currently prose-only). An\nunproved primary conjecture is honestly represented by this\ncontent-bearing class with no instance; creating an instance without\nproving the substrate monoid's rank-one structure would be laundering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.map_nsmul_of_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.map_nsmul_of_additive","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L139-L151","doc":"An additive counter on iterates of a single step `g` is linear in the\niterate count: `T (n • g) = n · T g`. This is the entire mathematical\nmechanism of the atomic discharge below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.map_zero_of_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.map_zero_of_additive","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L128-L137","doc":"An additive counter sends the empty computation to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.IsClock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.IsClock","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SubstrateClockUniqueness.lean#L115-L126","doc":"A **clock** on the substrate's computation monoid `M`: a `K`-valued\nstep-counter that (i) is additive under composition of computation\nsegments — the algebraic core of \"functorial under the substrate's\ncomposition of computation steps\" — and (ii) is not identically zero —\nthe algebraic shadow of cofinality (a counter that never registers any\ncomputation counts nothing). The order-theoretic clauses (strict\nmonotonicity for the braiding-induced ordering `≺_∞`, cofinality in the\nwell-founded computation order of `prop:ordering-jet-compatibility`) are\narchimedean-side refinements recorded in the audit; the downstream\nalgebra uses only (i)+(ii). ","signatureChunk":0}]}